Project     : Python Fundamentals
Module      : 06 - If Else
Author      : Kushendar
Repository  : python-fundamentals
Language    : Python 3

Description
-----------
This module introduces conditional statements in Python.

Conditional statements allow a program to make decisions
based on specific conditions. Depending on whether a
condition evaluates to True or False, the program can
execute different blocks of code.

Python provides the following conditional statements:

1. if
2. if...else
3. if...elif...else

Conditional statements are one of the most important
concepts in programming because they enable programs to
respond intelligently to different situations.

Learning Objectives
-------------------
1. Understand Boolean expressions.
2. Learn how to use the if statement.
3. Learn how to use if...else.
4. Learn how to use if...elif...else.
5. Build decision-making logic.
6. Display readable program output.

Functions Used
--------------
input()     Receive user input.
int()       Convert string to integer.
print()     Display information.

Expected Output
---------------
The program asks the user to enter an exam score and
determines the corresponding grade based on predefined
conditions.

Coding Style
------------
This module follows clean code principles and PEP 8
recommendations for readability, maintainability,
and professional software development.
=========================================================
"""


def main():
    """Main entry point of the program."""

    # =====================================================
    # Receive User Input
    # =====================================================

    student_name = input("Enter student name : ")
    exam_score = int(input("Enter exam score   : "))

    # =====================================================
    # Determine Grade
    # =====================================================

    if exam_score >= 90:
        grade = "A"
        description = "Excellent"

    elif exam_score >= 80:
        grade = "B"
        description = "Very Good"

    elif exam_score >= 70:
        grade = "C"
        description = "Good"

    elif exam_score >= 60:
        grade = "D"
        description = "Needs Improvement"

    else:
        grade = "E"
        description = "Failed"

    # =====================================================
    # Display Result
    # =====================================================

    print()
    print("=" * 70)
    print("Student Examination Result")
    print("=" * 70)

    print(f"Student Name : {student_name}")
    print(f"Exam Score   : {exam_score}")
    print(f"Grade        : {grade}")
    print(f"Result       : {description}")

    print("=" * 70)


if __name__ == "__main__":
    main()
